EAU\nST. LOUIS.\n\nSept.5, 1903.\n\nMiss Mary Louise Dalton,\nMissouri Historical Soey.,\nSt.Louis.\n\nMy dear Miss Dalton:--\nI think the following will fully answer\nyour inquiries, but if locations, months and dates are desired, […]\nmany can be furnished.\n\nPierre Ligueste de Laclede-- born 1724, emigrated to\nLouisiana 1755, founded St.Louis 1764, died 1778. I herewith\nquote from notes to which I referred:\n\n' The remainder of Laclede's life was spent in a strug-\ngle for existence.-- He was respected and beloved by all with\nwhom he came in contact -- He gave his all, and died without\naccumulation, for an enterprise that has resulted as he predicted,\n'in one of the finest cities of America!' He died June 20th,1778,\nat the mouth of the Arkansas river while en route from New Orleans\nto St.Louis.\n\nThe following year an expedition was sent to recover his\nbody; much to the chagrin of those who undertook this sad mission,\nthey found the mighty Mississippi had eaten into its banks, and\nclaimed the mortal remains of Laclede as being worthy to repose\nunder its turbid waters, alongside that of De Soto.\n\nVery truly yours,\nPierre Chouteau\n\nDictated.\n\nMissouri Historical\nSociety\nSaint Louis\n\nans\nSept 7-03","language":"en","uncertain":["Soey.","that","Pierre Chouteau","ans","Sept 7-03"],"translation":null}],"warnings":[],"timings":{"total":43732,"segment":6690,"match":498,"read":23719,"assemble":213,"transcribe":12574},"cost":{"usd":0.1698,"samCalls":1,"museCalls":20},"timeline":[{"t":0,"type":"start"},{"t":34,"type":"stage","id":"segment:active"},{"t":68,"type":"photo"},{"t":6723,"type":"segment"},{"t":6724,"type":"stage","id":"segment:done"},{"t":6724,"type":"stage","id":"match:active"},{"t":7222,"type":"match"},{"t":7222,"type":"stage","id":"match:done"},{"t":7223,"type":"stage","id":"read:active"},{"t":12898,"type":"read","id":"pair:p2~p7#0"},{"t":13247,"type":"read","id":"pair:p3~p5#0"},{"t":14431,"type":"read","id":"pair:p3~p8#0"},{"t":14753,"